{"name":"Green Eggs and Ham","hex":"#7cb68e","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"green","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of grass and leaves; a primary additive color midway between yellow and blue which is evoked by light between roughly 495–570 nm.","A member of a green party; an environmentalist."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a green hue.","Sickly, unwell."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/green"},{"term":"eggs","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of egg"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of egg"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/eggs"},{"term":"and","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Ansus."]},{"part":"Conjunction","definitions":["As a coordinating conjunction; expressing two elements to be taken together or in addition to each other.\nUsed simply to connect two noun phrases, adjectives or adverbs. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}\n\nSimply connecting two clauses or sentences. \n\nIntroducing a clause or sentence which follows on in time or consequence from the first.","Used simply to connect two noun phrases, adjectives or adverbs. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/and"}],"entries":[{"title":"Green Eggs and Ham","blocks":[{"text":"Green Eggs and Ham is a children's book by Dr. Seuss. It was published by the Beginner Books imprint of Random House on August 12, 1960. The book follows \"Sam-I-am\" as he follows an unnamed character, repeatedly requesting that he try a dish of green eggs and ham before the unnamed character eventually tries and approves of it."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/11/Green_Eggs_and_Ham.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Green_Eggs_and_Ham","wikidata":"Q2759523"},{"title":"Green Eggs and Ham (TV series)","blocks":[{"text":"Green Eggs and Ham, also known as Green Eggs and Ham: The Second Serving for its second season, is an American animated comedy adventure television series developed by Jared Stern for Netflix. It is based on the 1960 children's book by Dr. Seuss."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/a7/Green_Eggs_And_Ham_%28TV_Series%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Green_Eggs_and_Ham_(TV_series)","wikidata":"Q21463147"},{"title":"Ham","blocks":[{"text":"Ham is pork from a leg cut that has been preserved by wet or dry curing, with or without smoking. As a processed meat, the term ham includes both whole cuts of meat and ones that have been mechanically formed."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/Ham_%284%29.jpg/330px-Ham_%284%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ham","wikidata":"Q170486"},{"title":"Green","blocks":[{"text":"Green is the color between cyan and yellow on the visible spectrum. It has 295–350 different shades. It is evoked by light which has a dominant wavelength of roughly 495–570 nm. In subtractive color systems, used in painting and color printing, it is created by a combination of yellow and cyan; in the RGB color model, used on television and computer screens, it is one of the additive primary colors, along with red and blue, which are mixed in different combinations to create all other colors. By far the largest contributor to green in nature is chlorophyll, the chemical by which plants photosynthesize and convert sunlight into chemical energy. Many creatures have adapted to their green environments by taking on a green hue themselves as camouflage. Several minerals have a green color, including the emerald, which is colored green by its chromium content."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Champ_de_bl%C3%A9_C%C3%B4te-d%27Or_Bourgogne_avril_2014.jpg/330px-Champ_de_bl%C3%A9_C%C3%B4te-d%27Or_Bourgogne_avril_2014.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Green","wikidata":"Q3133"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fb/USMC-120302-M-PG598-001.jpg/500px-USMC-120302-M-PG598-001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fb/USMC-120302-M-PG598-001.jpg/1280px-USMC-120302-M-PG598-001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fb/USMC-120302-M-PG598-001.jpg/500px-USMC-120302-M-PG598-001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A woman reading and showing Green Eggs and Ham to children","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AUSMC-120302-M-PG598-001.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/The_Green_Eggs_and_Ham_Cafe_-_panoramio.jpg/500px-The_Green_Eggs_and_Ham_Cafe_-_panoramio.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/The_Green_Eggs_and_Ham_Cafe_-_panoramio.jpg/1280px-The_Green_Eggs_and_Ham_Cafe_-_panoramio.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/The_Green_Eggs_and_Ham_Cafe_-_panoramio.jpg/500px-The_Green_Eggs_and_Ham_Cafe_-_panoramio.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Green Eggs and Ham Cafe in the Seuss Landing theme park","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThe_Green_Eggs_and_Ham_Cafe_-_panoramio.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/60/Schinken-gekocht.jpg/500px-Schinken-gekocht.jp